From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: a view that begins in a granule its neighbour keeps takes its range out of the next one

free_ranges_insert_view finds the free range at the view's granule-rounded base. When the view begins inside a 64 KiB
granule a previous view still holds (an emulator splits placeholders on 16 KiB pages), that range ends exactly at the
granule, the clipping shrank the removal to nothing, and the free range the view runs into stayed listed under it.
A HashLink game mapped a 20 MiB section view at 0x2002c4000 after a 16 KiB view at 0x2002c0000; 0x2002d0000-0x2016c0000 stayed
free, the next allocation was given 0x2002d0000 and create_view asserted (view->protect & VPROT_SYSTEM), and the earlier emulator experiment (removed)
ended 24 s in (2026-10-15; record removed from the tree; in git history). Upstream places a new view inside one free range, so it never meets this case;
patch 1119 fixed the same split on the removal side. The range to shrink is the next one.

Host: tests/test_crash_replays.c ("free-range order": a view beginning in a kept granule leaves no free range under it).
Console: not yet run.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -1433,6 +1433,17 @@
 
     /* Free ranges addresses are aligned at granularity_mask while the views may be not. */
 
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* A view can begin in a granule the previous view keeps and run on into the next free range (an emulator splits its
+     * placeholders on 16 KiB pages). The range found ends at that granule and is not the one to shrink: the next free
+     * range stayed listed under the view, and a later allocation there made create_view assert (a 20 MiB view at
+     * 0x2002c4000 left 0x2002d0000-0x2016c0000 free, 2026-10-15). */
+    if (range->end <= view_base && next != free_ranges_end)
+    {
+        range = next;
+        next = range + 1;
+    }
+#endif
     if (range->base > view_base)
         view_base = range->base;
     if (range->end < view_end)
